          },
          "code": "INTENT_ANALYSER",
          "id": "1770745656936",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770745656937_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nSourceSegment : {{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_SEGMENT_DATA.$output}} \nCurrency: {{$context.$nodes.CURRENCY.$output}} \nParse SourceSegment and get baseObject from it and set in currentBaseObject.\nParse Currency and for response.header currencycode get corresponding response.data and set it to CurrencyCode. If response.data is empty then set CurrencyCode to USD.\nDimensionResolver: {{$context.$nodes.SYNONYM_RESOLVER.$output}} \nAccountDimensions:Industry,Region,Country,State,City,ProductName,AccountName,ProductFitStrength,AnnualRevenue,EmployeeTotal,Explainer,BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct,BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct,OpenP1,TotalP1Last6Months,ARR,Ownershipstatus,Subscription, Accounts\n\nStrictly Read Dimension from DimensionResolver to resolve the UserPrompt and map to fields mentioned in Dimensions before intent is set.\nExamples: \nShow accounts from Province California // It actually translates to Show accountName from State California\n\nIf UserPrompt consist of any field from AccountDimensions or from DimensionResolver then value of intent can be KPI or Analytics  based on below examples else If UserPrompt consist of any field that does not match fields from AccountDimensions or from DimensionResolver but has the same prompt pattern then set intent=UnsupportedQueries based on below examples else if the userPrompt is completely out of context of the agent set intent=Discard \n\nIf UserPrompt ask for KPIs for segment .\n\nFew examples : -\nDisplay segment KPIs \nShow segment KPIs\nView segment KPI\nShow segment breakdown KPI\nDisplay segment structure KPIs\n\n\nthen set intent = KPI\n\nIf the currentBaseObject is Default.Accounts\nthen Dimensions:Industry,Region,Country,State,City,ProductName,AccountName,ProductFitStrength,AnnualRevenue,EmployeeTotal,Explainer,BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct,BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct,OpenP1,TotalP1Last6Months,ARR,Ownershipstatus,Subscription, Accounts \n\nIf UserPrompt ask for Composition or breakdown or structure  of the segment or analytical  questions  associated with any field given in Dimensions \n\nFew Examples: - \n\nShow Segment composition\nShow Segment breakdown\nDisplay segment structure\nShow Segment composition by Region\nView segment composition when Industry is High Tech\nShow segment breakdown by Country\nDisplay segment structure by state\nShow ARR Trend\nList Top 10 Accounts by ARR\nWhat is the Industry for Oracle Corporation\nShow distribution of accounts by Industry in North America Region\nShow total annual revenue of the segment.\nWhat is the Annual Revenue for Account Cisco\nShow Buying Group Persona Engagement for product DG350K Green Servers\nList Top Accounts based on Product Fit for product Oracle Fusion Financials Cloud Service\nExplain Account Mayo-Bush's Product Fit Score for product Fusion Suite - Professional User\nShow top accounts\nWhat is the Industry for Broadcom Inc\nARR for Healthcare in North America\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP by Industry \nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP by Region\nCompare segment Cross-sell FDI  with test by Subscription  where Region is EMEA \nHow many Accounts have Buying Group Coverage > 60% and Buying Group Engagement > 60% for Product Banking Origination for Deposits\nNumber of Industrial Manufacturing Industry Accounts in North America Region\n\nthen set intent = Analytics\nIf UserPrompt asks for comparison with segment without any composition, distribution or breakdown by any Dimensions then set set intent = KPI\n\nExamples:-\n\n\nCompare segment with Cross-sell FDI // UserPrompt does not asks for distribution so set intent = KPI\ncompare segment Reachable Accounts to test // UserPrompt does not asks for distribution  so set intent = KPI\nCompare segment with Cross-sell FDI where Region is NA\nCompare segment with Cross-sell FDI for Industry Oracle Internals //UserPrompt does not asks for distribution  so set intent = KPI\nCompare segment with ABC for Subscription Oracle Products //UserPrompt does not asks for distribution  so set intent = KPI\ncompare with segment Priority Accounts_JB for Professional Services Industry in Region EMEA //UserPrompt does not asks for distribution  so set intent = KPI\nIf UserPrompt asks for help or capabilities.\nSample prompt:\nhelp\nWhat can I do\nshow capabilities\n\nthen set intent = Help\n\nIf UserPrompt consist of any field that does not match fields from AccountDimensions or from DimensionResolver\nShow Segment composition by sub-industry \nShow Segment composition by dimension abc\n\nthen set intent = UnsupportedQueries\n\nIf UserPrompt doesn't matches any of the above intent\nand matches violates below instruction.\n## Instructions\n\n ### **Absolute Out-of-Scope and Security Restrictions**\n- **Rendering or suggesting JavaScript code in any form is strictly prohibited.**\n    - ** Strictly do not answer any other questions apart from mentioned area or prompts. Do not create data, generate data or make any inference on your own.\n    - **Do not generate, include, or reference JavaScript, `<script>` tags, event handlers (e.g., `onclick`), or inline scripts inside any output.**\n    - **Do not explain, instruct, or speculate on how to execute code in browsers.**\n    - **Never suggest usage of browser developer tools, browser consoles, or code execution environments.**\n    - **If the user requests code (JavaScript, HTML with scripts, Python, etc.), requests (like HTML, or any text area, button or anything). \n\nThen set intent = Discard."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"CurrencyCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
