        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analytics Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770919684724"
          },
          "code": "ANALYTICS_INTENT",
          "id": "1770747049561",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770747049562_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nIf UserPrompt asks for comparision like below examples:-\n\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP by Industry\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell UBI to Unity by Region\nAnalyze the segment-wise cross-sell ABC to DEF by Country. \n\nThen set compare=Yes\nElse set compare=No"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"compare\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Help Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "HELP_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770815776274",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770815776277_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n If UserPrompt asks for metrics like below examples:-\n-Show metrics\n-Help metrics\n-Display metrics\n\nStrictly display below HTML format without any change and return. Do not make any inference or asks question to user :\n<p><strong>Supported metrics</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle;\">\n  <li>Number of Accounts</li>\n  <li>ARR</li>\n  <li>Product Fit Strength</li>\n  <li>Open P1s</li>\n  <li>Total P1s in Last 6 Months</li>\n</ul>\n\nIf UserPrompt asks for dimension like below examples:-\n\n-Show dimensions\n-Help Dimension\n-Display Dimensions\n\nStrictly display below HTML format without any change and return. Do not make any inference or asks question to user :\n<p><strong>Supported dimensions</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle;\">\n  <li>Industry</li>\n  <li>Region</li>\n  <li>Country</li>\n  <li>State</li>\n  <li>City</li>\n  <li>Subscription</li>\n  <li>Product Fit Strength</li>\n  <li>Product</li>\n  <li>Open P1s</li>\n  <li>Total P1s in Last 6 Months</li>\n</ul>\n\nWhen UserPrompt asks like below examples:-\n-Help\n-What can I do\n-Need Help\n-Show help\n-Display help\n\nStrictly display below HTML format without any change and return. Do not make any inference or asks question to user :\n<p>Type <strong>‘Help dimensions’</strong> to explore supported dimensions or <strong>‘Help metrics’</strong> to explore supported metrics.</p><br></br>\n<p><strong>Capabilities and usage guidelines</strong><br>\nThe Segment Insights Analyst provides the following insights and analytics for a segment.</p><br></br>\n<ol>\n  <li>\n    KPIs for the Segment such as Number of Accounts, Number of Contacts, ARR<br></br>\n    Example queries<br>\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>Show Segment KPIs</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li><br></br>\n<li>\n    Segment composition or distribution of accounts by dimensions such as Industry, Region and Product Fit Strength.\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>distribution of accounts by only one dimension at a time is supported</li>\n      <li>by default, the top 10 values of the queried dimension are listed</li>\n      <li>if you want to view more than the top 10 values of the queried dimension, specify the desired number of rows in the query (eg: Show distribution of Accounts by <strong>top 20</strong> Industries)</li>\n    </ul><br></br>\n    Example queries<br>\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>Show distribution of Accounts by top 20 Industries</li>\n      <li>Show distribution of Accounts by Region</li>\n      <li>Show distribution of Accounts by top 25 Subscriptions</li>\n      <li>Show distribution of Accounts by Product Fit Strength for Product &lt;PRODUCT_NAME&gt;</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li><br></br>\n<li>\n    Top accounts by supported metrics such as ARR\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>by default, the top 10 accounts are listed</li>\n      <li>by default, accounts are ordered by ARR</li>\n    </ul><br></br>\n    Example queries<br>\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>List top 25 Accounts</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li><br></br><li>\n    Comparison with another segment by KPIs\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>currently, only KPIs-based comparison is supported</li>\n    </ul><br></br>\n    Example queries<br>\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>Compare with Segment &lt;SEGMENT_NAME&gt;</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li><br></br>\n<li>\n    Analytics (KPIs, Segment composition, Top accounts) for a sub-segment created by filtering the current segment by dimensions such as Industry, Region and Product Fit.\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>filtering by only one value per dimension is supported</li>\n      <li>you must prefix the dimension name to the dimension value (Eg: <strong>Region</strong> EMEA, <strong>Industry</strong> Healthcare, <strong>Product Fit Strength</strong> Strong for <strong>Product</strong> PRODUCT1)</li>\n    </ul><br></br>\n    Example queries<br>\n    <ul style=\"list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 0;\">\n      <li>Show Segment KPIs for Industry Healthcare and Region EMEA</li>\n      <li>Show distribution of Accounts by Region for Industry Healthcare</li>\n      <li>List top 25 Accounts for Industry Healthcare and Region EMEA</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n</ol>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analytics Intent Decider"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "Yes": "1770920243803",
            "No": "1770920296371"
          },
          "code": "ANALYTICS_INTENT_DECIDER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770919684724",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770919684726_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.ANALYTICS_INTENT.$output.compare}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Comparison Analyser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771269552636"
          },
          "code": "COMPARISON_ANALYSER",
          "id": "1770920243803",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770920243805_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nCurrentSegment: {{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_SEGMENT_DATA.$output}} \n\nParse CurrentSegment and get items[0].name from JSON and set the value to CurrentSegmentName\n\nIf UserPrompt has Subscription than groupBy=ProductName, OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_ACTIVE'\nActive Subscription means OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_ACTIVE'.\nInactive or Expired Subscription means OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_INACTIVE'.\nIf groupBy has value, make selectAttribute=\"\"\n\nIf UserPrompt asks for comparison like below examples, consider extracting values for selectAttribute, groupBy, aggregate, filter, limit and orderBy from UserPrompt:-\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP by Industry // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Cross-sell FDI to ERP, selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell UBI to Unity by Region // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Cross-sell UBI to Unity,selectAttribute =, groupBy=Region , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell UBI to Unity by Subscription // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Cross-sell UBI to Unity,selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductName , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE'),orderBy=, limit=10\nCompare segment with segment Eloqua Segment by ARR  // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Eloqua Segment,selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(ARR='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=(ARR='DESC'), limit=10\nCompare segment with segment Eloqua Segment by OpenP1  // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Eloqua Segment,selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(OpenP1='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=(OpenP1='DESC'), limit=10\nAnalyse the segment-wise ABC to DEF by Country. // SourceSegment=ABC, TargetSegment=DEF,selectAttribute =, groupBy=Country, aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nCompare segment test1 with segment  ERP by Industry when Industry Industrial Manufacturing, Region NA // SourceSegment=test1, TargetSegment=ERP, selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(Industry='Industrial Manufacturing' and Region='NA'),orderBy=, limit=10\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"limit\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"orderBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"aggregate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"groupBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"selectAttribute\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"TargetSegment\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"SourceSegment\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analytics Intent Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ANALYTICS_INTENT_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770921426690",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770921426691_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "AnalyticsResponse : {{$context.$nodes.ANALYTICS_DATA.$output}} \nLimit: {{$context.$nodes.ANALYTICS_ANALYSER.$output.limit}} \nUserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nGroupByColumn: {{$context.$nodes.ANALYTICS_ANALYSER.$output.groupBy}} \nAggregateColumn: {{$context.$nodes.ANALYTICS_ANALYSER.$output.aggregate}} \nCurrencyCode: {{$context.$nodes.INTENT_ANALYSER.$output.CurrencyCode}} \n\nParse AnalyticsResponse and if \"errorMessage\" is not empty then display <br></br>errorMessage , display help section and return. Do not display below HTML table inside div.\nIf result.data is empty then strictly only display \"<br></br>There is no data for this query\" and display and display help section and return.Do not display below HTML table.\nDo not change any value in result.data, display as it is.\n- Populate the table using the AnalyticsResponse at: result.header and result.data\n- Use result.header[*].name for column headers and convert headers to uppercase.\n- Display of  result.data should be corresponding to result.header[*].name\n- For each row in result.data, map values by index to the corresponding header index.\n- Escape HTML special characters in all cell values.\n- If  result.headers contains  GroupByColumn  parse  corresponding result.data  for this column and replace any null or empty value with 'Not Available'\n- If header name is COUNT_AGG change it to Accounts\n-If  result.headers contains AccountName then make it first column\n- If header name is sum_aggr then use  AggregateName from AggregateColumn  and Display as last Column. \nFor Example - \nIf AggregateColumn value is  (OpenP1='Sum') //AggregateName=OpenP1\nIf AggregateColumn value is  (ARR='Sum') //AggregateName=ARR\n- If result.header[*].name  has \"Share\" then convert it to % of Total, and show after Accounts column, and these two should be last two columns. Strictly do not change value of corresponding result.data value.\n- Do not change the table structure; only insert headers/rows where marked.\n- Make Header name more user friendly, split words and Capitalize if possible. For example ACCOUNTNAME -> Account Name\n\nif result.data is not empty and before showing below HTML table display a line as reply of the UserPrompt . Use Limit in while constructing the line wherever limit is available in UserPrompt. Make the line grammatically correct. Do not repeat the prompt itself.\nIf ARR is part of header then append it with (<CurrencyCode>) // For example - ARR (USD)\nExample -\n1) If UserPrompt asks Show segment distribution by Region ,Then say \" Here is distribution of segment by Region .\n<br></br>\n<div style=\"width:100%; overflow-x:hidden;\">\n  <table role=\"table\" aria-label=\"Result table\"\n         style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; table-layout:fixed;\">\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <!-- BEGIN_HEADERS -->\n        <!-- Example: -->\n        <!-- <th scope=\"col\"\n             style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600; white-space:normal; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\">\n             count_aggr\n        </th> -->\n        <!-- END_HEADERS -->\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n<tbody>\n      <!-- BEGIN_ROWS -->\n      <!-- Example:\n      <tr style=\"background:#ffffff;\">\n        <td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; white-space:normal; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\">2</td>\n        <td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; white-space:normal; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\">Construction and Engineering</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr style=\"background:#fbfdff;\">\n        <td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; white-space:normal; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\">2</td>\n        <td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; white-space:normal; overflow-wrap:anywhere; word-break:break-word;\">Oracle Internal</td>\n      </tr>\n      -->\n      <!-- END_ROWS -->\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\nBelow is help section\nStrictly and always display below HTML in any scenario.\n<br></br><p>Type <strong>&lsquo;Help&rsquo;</strong> to view usage guidelines, explore supported dimensions and metrics, or see sample questions.</p>\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analytics Analyser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771258974655"
          },
          "code": "ANALYTICS_ANALYSER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770921426690",
          "id": "1770920296371",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770920296373_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nMemberSegmentData: {{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_SEGMENT_DATA.$output}} \nParse MemberSegmentData and append msid_ to items[0].id ans store in memberSegmentId\n\nIf UserPrompt asks for below samples , compute values for selectAttribute, groupBy, aggreagte, filter, limit:\n\n\n\nWhen ARR is there make orderBy=\"\"\nDimensions:Industry,Region,Country,State,City,ProductName,AccountName,ProductFitStrength,AnnualRevenue,EmployeeTotal,Explainer,BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct,BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct,OpenP1,TotalP1Last6Months,ARR \nDimensionResolver: {{$context.$nodes.SYNONYM_RESOLVER.$output}} \nMake sure that selectAttribute=\"\" if groupBy has values.\nPopulate groupBy only when composition, breakdown,structure or similar ask is there in UserPrompt.\nIf UserPrompt has Subscription than use ProductName and OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_ACTIVE'\nActive Subscription means OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_ACTIVE'.\nInactive or Expired Subscription means OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_INACTIVE'.\nOnly if UserPrompt asks for \"based on\" for ProductFitStrength then only include orderBy=(ProductFitStrength=DESC)\nIf groupBy has value, make selectAttribute=\"\"\nIf UserPrompt has distribution or composition but groupBy clause is not mentioned or identifyable then make groupBy=Industry\nUse instructions from DimensionResolver to convert into  matching Dimensions from the UserPrompt.\nExamples: \nShow accounts from Province California // It actually translates to Show accountName from State California\nAnalyse Dimensions  from UserPrompt.\nAnalyse below examples UserPrompt which should be considered for extracting values for selectAttribute, groupBy, aggregate, filter, limit and orderBy from UserPrompt - \n\nExamples -\nShow Segment composition // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow Segment breakdown // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nDisplay segment structure // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow Segment composition by Region // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Region , aggregate=(AccountID='Count') , filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow Segment composition by Subscription // selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductName , aggregate=(AccountID='Count') , filter=(OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE'),orderBy=, limit=10\nTop 5 accounts by Subscription // selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductName , aggregate=(AccountID='Count') , filter=(OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE'),orderBy=, limit=5\nView segment composition when Industry is High Tech, Region is NA // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(Industry='Industrial Manufacturing' and Region='NA'),orderBy=, limit=10\nShow Segment composition by Subscriptions when Industry Industrial Manufacturing, Region NA // selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductName, aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(Industry='Industrial Manufacturing' and Region='NA' and OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE'),orderBy=, limit=10 \nShow segment breakdown by Country // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Country, aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nDisplay segment structure by state // selectAttribute =, groupBy=state, aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow ARR Trend // selectAttribute =, groupBy=ARR , aggregate=(AccountName='Count') , filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow Segment composition by ProductFitStrength// selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductFitStrength , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nList Top 5 Accounts by ARR // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(ARR='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=5,\nShow top accounts // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(ARR='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow top accounts by OpenP1 // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(OpenP1='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow top accounts by OpenP1 for product Oracle RightNow Experience Routing Cloud Service // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(OpenP1='Sum'), filter=(ProductName='Oracle RightNow Experience Routing Cloud Service'),orderBy=, limit=10\nShow top accounts by TotalP1Last6Months // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(TotalP1Last6Months='Sum'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nShow top accounts by TotalP1Last6Months for subscription Revenue Management for Midsize Cloud Service // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName, aggregate=(TotalP1Last6Months='Sum'), filter=(ProductName='Revenue Management for Midsize Cloud Service' AND OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE'),orderBy=, limit=10\nList Top Accounts based on Product Fit for product Oracle Fusion Financials Cloud Service // selectAttribute=ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='Oracle Fusion Financials Cloud Service'), orderBy=(ProductFitStrength=DESC), limit=10\nList Top Accounts based on Product Fit for Industry Industrial Manufacturing , Region NA// selectAttribute=ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(Industry='Industrial Manufacturing' and Region='NA'),orderBy=(ProductFitStrength=DESC), limit=10\nShow distribution of Accounts by Product Fit Strength//selectAttribute=, groupBy=ProductFitStrength, aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=,orderBy=, limit=10\nExplain Product Fit for product Oracle Fusion Financials Cloud Service // selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='Oracle Fusion Financials Cloud Service'),orderBy=,limit=10\nExplain Account Mayo-Bush's Product Fit Score for product Fusion Suite - Professional User // selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='Fusion Suite - Professional User' AND AccountName='Mayo-Bush'),orderBy=,limit=10\nExplain Account Demo UNIVERSITY OF WYOMING's Product Fit Score for product  DG350K Green Servers// selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers' AND AccountName='Demo UNIVERSITY OF WYOMING'),orderBy=,limit=10\nExplain Product Fit for product Unity, Oracle Eloqua// selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='Unity' OR ProductName='Oracle Eloqua'),orderBy=,limit=10\nExplain Product Fit for product Fusion CDP and  Responsys// selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='Fusion CDP' AND ProductName='Responsys'),orderBy=,limit=10\nShow Buying Group Coverage for product DG350K Green Servers//selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers'),orderBy=,limit=10\nShow Buying Group Engagement for product DG350K Green Servers//selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers'),orderBy=,limit=10\nShow Buying Group Persona Coverage for product DG350K Green Servers//selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers'),orderBy=,limit=10\nShow Buying Group Persona Engagement for product DG350K Green Servers//selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers'),orderBy=,limit=10\nWhat is the Annual Revenue for Account Cisco // selectAttribute =AccountName,AnnualRevenue, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(AccountName='Cisco'),orderBy=,limit=10\nWhat are the top 10 accounts by Buying Group Coverage for SaaS - Other Fusion ERP and Applications - 0JWU// selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='SaaS - Other Fusion ERP and Applications - 0JWU'),orderBy=(BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct=DESC),limit=10\nWhat are the top 10 accounts by Buying Group Engagement for product DG350K Green Servers// selectAttribute =AccountName,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='DG350K Green Servers'),orderBy=(BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct=DESC),limit=10\nExplain for account  Demo COMPASS BANK CREDIT CARD SERVICES INC product fit strength  for product CategorySaaS - DataFox Supplier Intelligence - 08DH // selectAttribute =ProductFitStrength,Explainer,AccountName,ARR, groupBy=, aggregate=, filter=(ProductName='CategorySaaS - DataFox Supplier Intelligence - 08DH' AND AccountName='Demo COMPASS BANK CREDIT CARD SERVICES INC'),orderBy=,limit=10\nSegment composition by Subscription when Industry Healthcare, Professional Services Region NA, EMEA // selectAttribute =, groupBy=ProductName , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=((Industry='Healthcare' OR Industry='Professional Services') AND (Region='NA' OR Region='EMEA') AND (OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE')),orderBy=, limit=10\nSegment composition by Industry when Subscription ABC, DEF Region NA, EMEA // selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=((ProductName='ABC' OR ProductName='DEF') AND (Region='NA' OR Region='EMEA') AND (OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE')),orderBy=, limit=10\nSegment composition by Industry when Subscription Moniforce WebProbe Collector and  Siebel ePharma Call Activity Analytics Region NA, EMEA //selectAttribute =, groupBy=Industry , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=((ProductName='Moniforce WebProbe Collector' AND ProductName='Siebel ePharma Call Activity Analytics') AND (Region='NA' OR Region='EMEA') AND (OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE')),orderBy=, limit=10\nHow many Accounts have Buying Group Coverage > 60% and Buying Group Engagement > 60% for Product Incentive Compensation // selectAttribute =, groupBy= , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct > 60 AND BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct > 60 AND ProductName='Incentive Compensation'),orderBy=, limit=10\nList Accounts that have more than 2 Open P1 SRs // selectAttribute =, groupBy=AccountName , aggregate=(AccountID='Count'), filter=(OpenP1 > 2),orderBy=, limit=10"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"memberSegmentId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"orderBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"limit\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"aggregate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"groupBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"selectAttribute\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "KPI Analyser"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771437403504"
          },
          "code": "KPI_ANALYSER",
          "id": "1770925738181",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770925738181_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserPrompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nCurrentSegment: {{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_SEGMENT_DATA.$output}} \nAdditionalDimension: {{$context.$nodes.SYNONYM_RESOLVER.$output}} \n\nStrictly follow below instructions to resolve the field synonym in UserPrompt: \nIf userprompt includes word like Province,Canton,County then always replace with State .\nIf userprompt includes word like Product Fit,Fit then always replace with ProductFitStrength .\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Coverage, Buying Group Role Coverage then always replace with BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct .\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Engagement, Buying Group Role Engagement then always replace with BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct .\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Persona Coverage then always replace with BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct .\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Persona Engagement then always replace with BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct .\nIf userprompt includes word like Open P1 SRs,Open P1 Tickets,Open Sev1s,Open Sev1 SRs,Open Sec1 Tickets,Open Critical SRs,Open Critical Tickets then always replace with OpenP1 .\nIf userprompt includes word like Total P1s in Last 6 Months,Total P1 SRs in Last 6 Months,Total P1 Tickets in Last 6 Months,Total Sev1s in Last 6 Months,Total Sec1 Tickets in Last 6 Months,Total Critical SRs in Last 6 Months then always replace with TotalP1Last6Months .\nIf userprompt includes word like status then always replace with OwnershipStatus .\nIf userprompt includes word like Account, Account name then always replace with AccountName .\nIf userprompt includes word like Subscription ,Product, Product name then always replace with ProductName .\nIf userprompt includes word like Annual Revenue then always replace with AnnualRevenue .\n\nRead instructions from AdditionalDimension and replace dimension in UserPrompt accordingly\nParse CurrentSegment and get items[0].name from JSON and set the value to CurrentSegmentName\nParse CurrentSegment and append msid_ to get items[0].id from JSON and set the value to CurrentSegmentId\nIf UserPrompt has Subscription than use ProductName and OwnershipStatus value is 'ORA_ACTIVE'\nIf UserPrompt asks for below samples , compute values for  filter:\n\nFew examples UserPrompt which should be considered for extracting values for  filter: - \n\nShow Segment KPIs when Industry High Technology, Region NA // filter=\"(Industry='High Technology' and Region='NA')\"\nShow KPI having state Florida, Country as USA , arr more than 100 // filter=\"(state='Florida' and Country='USA' and arr>100)\"\nShow segment KPI with accountname COMPASS BANK CREDIT CARD SERVICES INC // filter=\"(accountName='COMPASS BANK CREDIT CARD SERVICES INC')\"\nShow Segment KPIs for subscription Oracle Insurance Revenue Management and Billing //  filter=\"(ProductName='Oracle Insurance Revenue Management and Billing' AND OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE')\"\nShow segment kpi // filter=\"\"\nShow Segment KPIs when Buying Group Coverage > 60% and Buying Group Engagement > 60% // filter = \"(BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct > 60 AND BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct > 60)\"\nset compare=FALSE\n\nFew examples of compare KPIs in user prompt \nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Cross-sell FDI to ERP,filter=\"\"\nCompare segment with segment Cross-sell FDI to ERP when Industry  Industrial Manufacturing, Region NA // SourceSegment={value of CurrentSegmentName}, TargetSegment=Cross-sell FDI to ERP, filter=(Industry='Industrial Manufacturing' and Region='NA')\nCompare segment test1 with segment  ERP by Industry when Region EMEA // SourceSegment=test1, TargetSegment=ERP, filter=(Region='EMEA')\nCompare segment test1 with segment  ERP for subscription Oracle Insurance Revenue Management and Billing //  SourceSegment=test1, TargetSegment=ERP, filter=\"(ProductName='Oracle Insurance Revenue Management and Billing AND OwnershipStatus='ORA_ACTIVE')\"\nset compare=TRUE\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"CurrentSegmentId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"TargetSegment\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"SourceSegment\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"compare\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
