          "code": "COMPARE_ANALYTICS_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1771306617841",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771306617842_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SourceCompareData: {{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_COMPARE_DATA.$output}}\nTargetCompareData: {{$context.$nodes.TARGET_COMPARE_DATA.$output}}\nSourceSegmentName: {{$context.$nodes.COMPARISON_ANALYSER.$output.SourceSegment}} \nTargetSegmentName: {{$context.$nodes.COMPARISON_ANALYSER.$output.TargetSegment}} \nGroupByColumn: {{$context.$nodes.COMPARISON_ANALYSER.$output.groupBy}} \n\nAdd attribute  \"segmentName:\"<SourceSegmentName>\" to SourceCompareData parallel  to \"errorMessage\"  but do not display it.\nAdd attribute \"segmentName:\"<TargetSegmentName>\"  toTargetCompareData  parallel  to \"errorMessage\" but do not display it.\n\n\n\nParse SourceCompareData and if \"errorMessage\" is not empty then display errorMessage in bold and return. Do not display below HTML table.\nParse TargetCompareData and if \"errorMessage\" is not empty then display errorMessage in bold and return. Do not display below HTML table.\n\n- Segment names shown in the grouped header row (use the provided segmentName values).\n- Dimension column: GroupByColumn\n- If result.data in SourceCompareData or TargetCompareData  corresponding to GroupByColumn in headers  is empty replace it with 'Not Available'\n- If header name is COUNT_AGG change it to Accounts \n-Show share with same value, and change header of share to % of Total . Replace with 0 if value is not available.\n-Make Header name more user friendly, split words and Capitalize if possible. For example ACCOUNTNAME -> Account Name\nBefore showing below HTML display a line as reply of the UserPrompt . Use Limit in while constructing the line wherever limit is available in UserPrompt. Make the line grammatically correct. Do not repeat the prompt itself.\nExample -\n1) If UserPrompt asks Show segment distribution by Region ,Then say \" Here is distribution of segment by Region .\n<br></br>\n\n<div style=\"width:100%; overflow-x:auto;\"><table role=\"table\" aria-label=\"<GroupByColumn> distribution comparison\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; min-width:760px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\"><thead><!-- Group header row --><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\"></th><th scope=\"colgroup\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:center; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">{{segmentAName}} <!-- e.g., Cross-sell IC to ERP HCM --></th><th scope=\"colgroup\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:center; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">{{segmentBName}} <!-- e.g., Cross-sell IC to SCM --></th></tr><!-- Column header row --><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\"><GroupByColumn></th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">Accounts</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">Share</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">Accounts</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; background:#f6f8fa; font-weight:600;\">Share</th></tr></thead><tbody><!-- LLM INSTRUCTIONS FOR ROWS: 1) Parse both SourceCompareData and TargetCompareData JSON. 2) Build an ordered list of <GroupByColumn>: <GroupByColumn> = union of <GroupByColumn> from both segments (keep segment A order first, then append any missing from segment B) 3) For each <GroupByColumn>: accountsA = count in segment A else 0 accountsB = count in segment B else 0 4) Alternate row backgrounds: row 1: #ffffff row 2: #fbfdff row 3: #ffffff ... --><!-- BEGIN_ROWS_LOOP --><tr style=\"background:{{rowBackground}};\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left;\">{{GroupByColumn}}</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left;\">{{accountsA}}</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left;\">{{shareA}}%</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left;\">{{accountsB}}</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left;\">{{shareB}}%</td></tr><!-- END_ROWS_LOOP --><!-- Optional error block (render only if needed) <tr style=\"background:#fff5f5;\"><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #d0d7de; padding:8px 10px; text-align:left; color:#7a1c1c;\">Error: {{errorMessage}}</td></tr> --></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAlways display below HTML after the table\n<br></br><p>Type <strong>&lsquo;Help&rsquo;</strong> to view usage guidelines, explore supported dimensions and metrics, or see sample questions.</p>\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
