          "code": "KPI_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1771441701355",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771441701356_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SegmentKPI : {{$context.$nodes.KPI_DATA.$output}} \nSegmentName: {{$context.$nodes.KPI_ANALYSER.$output.SourceSegment}} \nCurrencyCode: {{$context.$nodes.INTENT_ANALYSER.$output.CurrencyCode}} \nParse SegmentKPI and if \"errorMessage\" is not empty then display errorMessage in bold and return. Do not display below HTML statement below.\n\nParse SegmentKPI and substitute value from SegmentKPI in  below html statement and display below html statement. Do not make any inference and display the statement as it is, without checking the values. If <result.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data> or <result.Default.Accounts.data> or  <result.Default.Contacts.data> is blank replace with 0.\nConvert result.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data value   into a human-readable format using thousand (K), million (M), and billion (B). Round to 2 decimal places.\n\n<html> This segment consists of <b><result.Default.Accounts.data></b> accounts and <b><result.Default.Contacts.data></b> contacts representing an annual recurring revenue of  <b>{CurrencyCode} <result.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data></b> <br></br> <html>\n\nStrictly display below HTML\n<br></br><p>Type <strong>&lsquo;Help&rsquo;</strong> to view usage guidelines, explore supported dimensions and metrics, or see sample questions.</p>\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
