            "name": "KPI Compare Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "KPI_COMPARE_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1771443236627",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771443236629_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CompareSegmentKPI : {{$context.$nodes.COMPARE_SEGMENT_KPI.$output}} \nCurrencyCode: {{$context.$nodes.INTENT_ANALYSER.$output.CurrencyCode}} \nSourceSegmentName: {{$context.$nodes.KPI_ANALYSER.$output.SourceSegment}} \nTargetSegmentName: {{$context.$nodes.KPI_ANALYSER.$output.TargetSegment}} \nParse CompareSegmentKPI and if \"errorMessage\" is not empty then display errorMessage in bold and return. Do not display below HTML statement below.\n\nParse CompareSegmentKPI and store \"result\" from JSON  in CompareSegmentResult\n\nConvert result.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data value   into a human-readable format using thousand (K), million (M), and billion (B). Round to 2 decimal places.\nGet commonAccounts from CompareSegmentResult and store in CommonAccountResult. If CommonAccountResult is null or empty show it as {CurrencyCode} 0.\nIf <CompareSegmentResult.source.Default.Contacts.data> or <CompareSegmentResult.source.Default.Accounts.data> or <CompareSegmentResult.source.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data> or <CompareSegmentResult.target.Default.Accounts.data> or <CompareSegmentResult.target.Default.Contacts.data> or <CompareSegmentResult.target.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data> is null or blank replace it with 0.\nJust display the below HTML statement. Do not make any inference. If any value is empty replace with 0. Do not show \"[\" or \"]\" in data while populating html statement. Make sure only numbers and segmentname are in bold. \n\n<html>{SourceSegmentName} consists of <b><CompareSegmentResult.source.Default.Accounts.data></b> accounts and <b><CompareSegmentResult.source.Default.Contacts.data></b> contacts representing an annual recurring revenue of  <b>{CurrencyCode} <CompareSegmentResult.source.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data></b><br></br>{TargetSegmentName} consists of <b><CompareSegmentResult.target.Default.Accounts.data></b> accounts and <b><CompareSegmentResult.target.Default.Contacts.data></b> contacts representing an annual recurring revenue of  <b>{CurrencyCode} <CompareSegmentResult.target.*AccountProductIntelligence*.data></b>.There are <b>{CommonAccountResult} accounts common </b>to both segments.<html>\n\nAlways display below HTML after the table\n<br></br><p>Type <strong>&lsquo;Help&rsquo;</strong> to view usage guidelines, explore supported dimensions and metrics, or see sample questions.</p>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Synonym Resolver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770745656936"
          },
          "code": "SYNONYM_RESOLVER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770745656936",
          "id": "1771308634019",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776681288008",
              "name": "AccountDimension",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "[Industry,Region,Country,State,City,ProductName,AccountName,ProductFitStrength,AnnualRevenue,EmployeeTotal,Explainer,BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct,BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct,BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct,BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct,OpenP1,TotalP1Last6Months,ARR,Ownershipstatus,Subscription, Accounts]"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771308644195",
              "name": "Synonym",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "If userprompt includes word like Province,Canton,County then always return State as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Product Fit,Fit then always return ProductFitStrength as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Coverage, Buying Group Role Coverage then always return BuyingGroupRoleCoveragePct as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Engagement, Buying Group Role Engagement then always return BuyingGroupRoleEngagementPct as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Persona Coverage then always return BuyingGroupPersonaCoveragePct as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Buying Group Persona Engagement then always return BuyingGroupPersonaEngagementPct as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Open P1 SRs,Open P1 Tickets,Open Sev1s,Open Sev1 SRs,Open Sec1 Tickets,Open Critical SRs,Open Critical Tickets then always return OpenP1 as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Total P1s in Last 6 Months,Total P1 SRs in Last 6 Months,Total P1 Tickets in Last 6 Months,Total Sev1s in Last 6 Months,Total Sec1 Tickets in Last 6 Months,Total Critical SRs in Last 6 Months then always return TotalP1Last6Months as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like status then always return OwnershipStatus as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Account, Account name then always return AccountName as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Subscription ,Product, Product name then always return ProductName as Dimension.\nIf userprompt includes word like Annual Revenue then always return AnnualRevenue as Dimension."
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
